WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.969 --> 00:00:05.399
With so many storylines to wrap up and character
arcs to complete, the final season of Game

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.940
of Thrones was bound to make bold moves that
not everyone agreed with.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:13.640
Such was the case on the latest episode of
the fantasy drama, "The Last of the Starks,"

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:18.420
which has fans sulking, stamping their feet,
and setting the internet ablaze with criticism.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:20.140
Major spoilers ahead!

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:24.920
The fourth episode of season 8 started out
strong, picking up after the jaw-dropping

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:28.700
victory over the Night King and his White
Walker army at the Battle of Winterfell to

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:33.360
show the survivors laughing, carousing, and
commending one another for their bravery and

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:33.860
strength.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:38.720
Daenerys made Gendry Lord of Storm's End,
Tormund guzzled down wine like it was going

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:42.840
out of style, and the Lannister brothers goofed
off playing a drinking game with Brienne of

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.020
Tarth that eventually led to a steamy romance
scene.

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:51.200
Sadly, the merriment fizzled out as quickly
as it came and "The Last of the Starks" ended

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:54.200
up disappointing tons of die-hard Game of
Thrones fans.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:55.820
"My heart is broken!"

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.140
"Don't touch me."

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:02.520
For starters, many kicked up a fuss over the
increasingly strained dynamic between Daenerys

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:07.070
and Jon Snow, who recently revealed to his
lady love that he's really her nephew and

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:09.100
the rightful heir to the Iron Throne.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:13.500
Some felt that the tension between the two
— Daenerys wants the Iron Throne more than

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:18.190
anything and firmly requests Jon not tell
anyone about his true parentage, while Jon

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:22.280
doesn't have any interest in ruling the Seven
Kingdoms and tells Dany that he'll always

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:24.940
bend the knee to her — has become unbearable.

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:29.280
One fan took to Twitter to write that it's
"annoying" that Jon is letting his love for

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:35.060
Daenerys influence his decisions, while others
said that the Dany-Jon conflict is "frustrating"

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:38.920
because it seems a marriage between the two
would resolve problems and allow them both

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:40.340
to get what they desire.

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:45.540
Dany's "recklessness" and Jon's "naïveté"
were also sore spots for some fans.

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:49.760
Of course, that's just the tip of the dragon's
wing of problems fans had.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.960
Viewers were heartbroken to see another one
of Daenerys' dragons plummet to his death

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:59.240
— this time Rhaegal, shot down by Euron
Greyjoy as Dany and her allied forces stormed

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:00.140
King's Landing.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:05.220
One fan wrote on Twitter that Rhaegal's death
was a "lazy" surprise, tweeting,

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:09.560
"Like nobody saw the massive fleet of ships
that everybody then saw immediately?

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:12.900
Nobody thought to scout when you know they
have a massive fleet of ships?"

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.600
Another said in response,

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:19.350
"They've written themselves into a corner,
and have gotten incredibly lazy/sloppy with

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:19.880
the story.

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:24.640
They could have easily killed Rhaegal [because]
Dany saw the ships, and in her hubris went

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:26.900
in charging not knowing about all the arrows.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.240
Simple change, much more plausible."

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:33.500
Rhaegal's gnarly demise wasn't the only shocking
death in the episode.

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:38.010
As punishment for Daenerys not giving up her
crusade for the Iron Throne, and to send her

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:42.120
a message about what she'll do if she doesn't
surrender, Cersei Lannister had the Mountain

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:46.670
behead Dany's loyal adviser Missandei, who
had been taken prisoner when Euron and his

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:48.940
Iron Fleet ambushed Dany's ships.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:54.140
Unsurprisingly, Missandei's murder sent shockwaves
through social media, with many stating that

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:58.950
she "deserved so much better" and others expressing
distress over the fact that her lover Grey

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:01.380
Worm is now living his worst nightmare.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:05.660
The indignation didn't stop there — more
Thrones fans let it be known that they were

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:10.480
disappointed over Jon sending his direwolf
Ghost north of the Wall without even patting

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:15.680
his head to say goodbye, Tyrion and Varys
contemplating committing treason and considering

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:20.320
withdrawing their support for Dany in favor
of Jon after they learn who Jon truly is,

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:25.270
and Jaime abandoning Brienne and heading for
Cersei in King's Landing shortly after the

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:27.760
two knights shared several intimate evenings
together.

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:32.780
All this anger and sadness over Season 8,
Episode 4 of Game of Thrones has resulted

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:37.960
in a grim consequence: the episode is currently
the second-lowest-rated Thrones installment

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:40.720
in history based on Rotten Tomatoes reviews.

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:46.350
The episode stands at a 61 percent approval
rating on the aggregator site, coming in only

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:51.780
a few percentage points above the disturbing
season 5 episode "Unbowed, Unbent, Unbroken,"

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:53.820
which earned a score of 54 percent.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:59.120
Game of Thrones has only two episodes remaining
in its entire run, and it's anyone's guess

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:03.440
how the show is going to bounce back from
this perceived low point — especially now

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:08.220
that Daenerys is on the brink, Team Targaryen
is down two important members, Dany's trusted

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:12.239
advisers could turn their backs on her at
any moment, and Jaime is plotting something

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:12.740
big.

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:17.350
For the sake of viewers' wellbeing and in
hopes that Thrones will go out on a high note,

00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:21.780
we have our fingers crossed that the upcoming
episode doesn't ruffle quite as many feathers

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:22.920
as this one did.

